11-28T09:20:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T14:15:11Z","closed_at":"2026-04-21T13:54:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nNot present in 4.4.1\nPresent in 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11, Godot 4.5.1 stable (double precision)\n\n### Issue description\n\nArea3Ds collide-able area is delayed by 1 frame when physics are done on a separate thread.\n\nThis is recorded in 4.4.1 stable, in a double-precision build. The raycast detects the Area3D buttons properly.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a80dbdf-7bcb-46e1-80b8-cac385addb10\n\nThis is recorded in 4.5.1 stable, in a double-precision build, using the same project. The raycast doesn't detect the Area3D in the proper position. Through my testing I found that the buttons can be pressed as if they are lagging behind by 1 frame.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/889fc478-5676-4516-9ee6-d575283a14cd\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Area3D as a child of a PhysicsBody (in this case, a RigidBody)\n- Raycast3D as a child of the same physics body\n- ProjectSetting `physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread` set to `true`\n- As the PhysicsBody moves, the Area3D's detectable area lags behind by 1 frame. (movement in MRP is produced in a \"correct\" way, by controlling linear velocity in _integrate_forces)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp-raycast-issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23820079/mrp-raycast-issue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com